From b5dd57de8e3fb4c5028cda56c2b85b9fb95d80e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:40:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] power: enable RPM-coordinated MSM8660 system collapse

Use the prepared conservative RPMRS sleep set before Hikari system collapse and arm SAW in RPM-notified mode. On abort, restore the conservative untimed sleep set; after a completed collapse, return the coordinator to idle after hardware state is restored.

Keep CPU idle on the existing standalone SAW path.
---
